<task id="205a" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Auth-v4 runtime-contract integration — row A38 (H4/H4-shared credential-type seam (FR-39) — secret-free omit)</title>
    <phase>Phase Pre-Live-Fire — Auth-v4 runtime-contract integration (task 205)</phase>
    <gate>ready</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Per project CLAUDE.md rigor table + §8.5 TEST-MODIFYING override: task tags include `auth` (H4 KV secrets credential-type seam) and modifies `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/**` + adds unit + integration tests under `tests/**` — TEST-MODIFYING override triggers unconditional FULL rigor (code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5). Credential-selection surface is auth-blast-radius: a wrong omit-set produces the "secret beneath MI-FIC absorbing a broken FIC with green health" failure mode (remediation plan §8) which reviewers cannot detect at runtime. Explicit escalation trigger per project CLAUDE.md §Human Escalation Triggers: any partial omit-set discovery (multiple upsert sites beyond `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs:74`) MUST STOP + re-scope; incomplete omit is worse than no change.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>fable</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Explicit user directive per remediation plan §8 Fable/Opus tier posture: "A38 + A42 on Fable/Opus (credential-selection seam + cross-worktree reconciliation — auth-tagged, FULL rigor, code-review + adr-check unconditional); rest Sonnet-5 @ high". Justified by (a) credential-logic blast radius (every future customer's authentication path), (b) cross-worktree consumption of auth-v4's DELIVERED §9.1 sentinel ruling + §10.1 Δ1/Δ2 addendum, (c) partial-closure reasoning for A30 sentinel contract (H4 half here + H7/task-142 half in-scope with an escalation escape hatch), (d) Model 1 vs Model 2 fleet-consistency semantics (N per-customer vaults) that Sonnet-5 literal-execution posture would under-generalize.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Code-only under `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/**` + tests under `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/**`; disjoint from A42's H3 handler seam (`Handlers/EntraAppReg/**`). Both may run concurrently as background agents per remediation plan §7 "S2 (task 205): A35 → { A38 ∥ A42 } → A39". No `.claude/**` writes (main-session-only per Sub-Agent Write Boundary root §3).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>A35 (already landed via merge commit `28c2c1b38`); consumes auth-v4 §9.1 sentinel ruling + §10.1 Δ1/Δ2 that A35 brought in-tree</deps>
    <tags>provisioning, auth, code, control-plane, credential-seam, fr-39</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4h (per punch row A38 in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md`; remediation plan §8 confirms)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Apply punch row A38 from `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` — the H4/H4-shared credential-type seam (FR-39) omit contract on secret-free environments. On secret-free envs, OMIT (never sentinel per §9.1 — sentinel produces opaque `AADSTS7000215` at runtime) three KV manifest entries: `BFF-API-ClientSecret`, `ServiceBus-ConnectionString`, `AiSearch--AdminKey`. Verified pre-work state: `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs:74` still upserts `AiSearch--AdminKey` (`FromBicepOutput`); the other two entries' source sites have NOT been grep-confirmed and MUST be located first (executor obligation per row A38). The positive migration marker is a KV resource tag OR a provisioning-state field, NEVER a value written into the credential slot itself. This row partially closes A30's sentinel contract (the H4 half); the H7/task-142 half is IN SCOPE HERE EXPLICITLY per AUTH-V4-RESPONSE naming both H4 AND H7 — if the H7/task-142 half cannot be closed within the 4h budget, ESCALATE with a proposed A44.5 row rather than silently dropping. Acceptance MUST state Model 1 (shared KV, single vault) vs Model 2 (per-customer `kv-{customerId}-{secretsVer}` × N vaults) behavior explicitly, including how the secret-free marker is applied consistently across N per-customer vaults (fleet-consistency gap per remediation plan §5.3 — a missed tag on one vault is itself a silent-skip failure). Executor MUST NOT regress A23's clobber guard (skip-if-absent + never-declared) — A38 modifies the SAME manifest area. Amend punch-list annotations. Do NOT commit — main session handles commit after review.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE L2 control-plane handler author + KV secrets manifest expert + credential-selection seam specialist. Expert in: `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs` interim body + the `IKvSecretManifest` contract + the FileKvSecretManifest Phase-H generator seam (task 084); the `KvSecretEntry(name, operation, valueSource)` record + `KvSecretOperation` (Upsert/SkipIfAbsent/etc.) + `KvSecretValueSource` (FromBicepOutput/FromExistingKvSecret/FromRunParameter/Generated); H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler + H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler dispatch model (Model 1 shared vault vs Model 2 per-customer vault); ADR-028 A4 secret-free BFF-identity contract + §9.1 sentinel ruling (OMIT-is-the-signal, never sentinel — sentinel → opaque `AADSTS7000215`); FR-39 pluggable credential seam + FR-40 invariant I6; A23 clobber guard (`skip-if-absent` + `never-declared`); §6.5 conflict resolution record 2026-08-25 (prong 1 = never-create/seed/restore secret-free-env `BFF-API-ClientSecret`; prong 2 = purge-protection of soft-deleted rollback copies through 2026-11-23; `Dataverse-ClientSecret` STAYS as Q3 Path A rollback copy until 2026-11-23 sunset — NEVER omit that one).</role>

  <goal>The three secret-free-target manifest entries are OMITTED from the manifest that `IKvSecretManifest.ReadAsync(...)` returns on secret-free environments: (1) `BFF-API-ClientSecret` — source site located + omitted; (2) `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` — source site located + omitted; (3) `AiSearch--AdminKey` — source site `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs:74` omitted. Positive migration marker is applied to Key Vault as a resource tag OR to a `sprk_dataverseenvironment` provisioning-state field — NEVER as a value in the credential slot itself (§9.1 sentinel ruling). Unit tests + integration tests assert: (a) manifest EXCLUDES the three entries when the env is secret-free (Model 1 shared vault AND Model 2 per-customer vault paths both covered); (b) manifest still INCLUDES them when explicit Q3 Path A rollback mode is on (`Dataverse-ClientSecret` per §6.5 record stays independently; the three A38 targets return only under explicit rollback flag); (c) marker application is idempotent + fleet-consistent — for Model 2, marker is applied uniformly across N per-customer vaults + a missed tag on one vault is detected (candidate T8 profile-coherence probe or manifest-linter class per remediation plan §5.3). Acceptance criteria explicitly cover Model 1 shared-KV path AND Model 2 per-customer N-vaults path. H7/task-142 half of A30 sentinel contract closed (or escalated with A44.5 proposal if separate scope). `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/` + `dotnet test src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/` succeed. A23 clobber guard (`skip-if-absent` + `never-declared`) NOT regressed — grep-confirm both terms still present + still exercised by tests. `FromBicepOutput` / `FromExistingKvSecret` / `FromRunParameter` classifications for entries that STAY (Cosmos, `Dataverse-ClientSecret` per Q3 Path A) are UNCHANGED — only the three omit-target entries change.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Auth-v4 §10 addendum Δ1/Δ2 + §9.1 sentinel ruling landed in-tree via A35 (merge commit `28c2c1b38`, 2026-08-25). Dev environment cut over to MI-FIC 2026-08-24: `spaarke-bff-dev` runs `Graph__Credentials__Order__0=ManagedIdentityFederated` (sole entry) + `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` (fail-fast); `BFF-API-ClientSecret` + lowercase alias deleted from KV 17:14Z (soft-deleted to 2026-11-22, not purged); E-3 CLOSED. Yet r1's `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs:74` still upserts `AiSearch--AdminKey` on every H4 run — the exact migration-undo vector remediation plan §5 item 3 names. On a fresh Model 2 stamp booting under `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true`, a re-seeded admin-key/SB-conn/BFF-client-secret from H4 either (a) fails-fast the boot when the fail-fast fires, or (b) — worse — silently sits BENEATH MI-FIC absorbing a broken FIC with green health signals (remediation plan §8 "boots-but-dead / silently WRONG" failure mode). A38 closes this vector at the manifest source. §9.1 rules OUT the tempting shortcut of writing a sentinel value into the slot instead of omitting: Entra returns opaque `AADSTS7000215` on sentinel resolution, indistinguishable from a real secret misconfiguration in operator triage. OMIT-is-the-signal; the migration marker must live outside the credential slot (KV resource tag or `sprk_dataverseenvironment` state field). Model 1 (single shared vault) is trivially fleet-consistent; Model 2 fans out to N per-customer `kv-{customerId}-{secretsVer}` vaults where a missed tag on one vault is itself a silent-skip failure (remediation plan §5.3 fleet-consistency gap). A38 also partially closes A30 (sentinel contract) — the H4 half here; the H7/task-142 half is EXPLICITLY IN SCOPE per AUTH-V4-RESPONSE naming both. §6.5 record (APPROVED owner 2026-08-25) confirms: `BFF-API-ClientSecret` Path C (pivot to comply with ADR-028 A4-as-amended, prong 1 = never-create/seed/restore in secret-free envs); `Dataverse-ClientSecret` Path A (time-boxed to 2026-11-23) — the latter STAYS unconditionally in the manifest as rollback copy. A38's omit-set is exactly three: `BFF-API-ClientSecret`, `ServiceBus-ConnectionString`, `AiSearch--AdminKey`. NOT `Dataverse-ClientSecret`. NOT `Cosmos*` (Cosmos entries are `FromBicepOutput` and unaffected). Executor must grep-locate the `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` + `BFF-API-ClientSecret` source sites FIRST: as of 2026-08-25 verification only `AiSearch--AdminKey` was grep-confirmed inside `StaticKvSecretManifest`; the other two sites are TBD (may be `StaticKvSecretManifest` also, or `FileKvSecretManifest`, or a distinct seed path). An incomplete omit-set is worse than no change — a residual site keeps the sentinel-vs-omit fight going. A23 clobber guard (skip-if-absent + never-declared) is in the same manifest area and MUST NOT regress.</background>
