  <constraints>
    <constraint source="auth-v4 §9.1 sentinel ruling (verified in remediation plan §5 SF-16)">MUST NOT sentinel any of the three secret entries on secret-free envs. Sentinel value written into the credential slot produces opaque `AADSTS7000215` at runtime — indistinguishable from a real secret misconfiguration in operator triage. OMIT is the signal. Migration marker MUST live outside the credential slot: KV resource tag OR provisioning-state field on `sprk_dataverseenvironment`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="punch row A23 (already-applied clobber guard)">MUST NOT regress the `skip-if-absent` + `never-declared` clobber guard in the manifest generator. A38 modifies the SAME manifest area (`KvSecretsPopulation/**`). Grep-confirm both terms still present in the manifest source(s) + still exercised by the corresponding tests AFTER the omit-set edit.</constraint>
    <constraint source="punch row A38 acceptance obligation (Model 1 vs Model 2)">MUST state Model 1 (single shared KV vault) vs Model 2 (per-customer `kv-{customerId}-{secretsVer}` × N vaults) behavior explicitly in acceptance criteria + in code comments / docstrings on the omit-branch. Manifest generator produces one manifest per environment; Model 2 fan-out is at the H4 dispatch level.</constraint>
    <constraint source="remediation plan §5.3 fleet-consistency gap (verifier addition)">For Model 2, the secret-free migration marker MUST be applied consistently across N per-customer vaults. A missed tag on one vault is itself a silent-skip failure. Acceptance MUST describe how the missed-tag case is detected: candidate T8 profile-coherence probe (cross-check tag vs live settings) OR manifest-linter class (per remediation plan §5.3 + §5 catalog SF-3 successor). If the detector cannot land within the 4h budget, file a follow-up row in `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` (do NOT silently defer — silence is the exact anti-pattern §9.1 exists to prevent).</constraint>
    <constraint source="AUTH-V4-RESPONSE A30 sentinel scope (H4 + H7)">MUST include the H7/task-142 half of A30's sentinel contract IN SCOPE. If the H7/task-142 half cannot be closed within the 4h budget (e.g. because H7 modifies a substantially different handler surface), ESCALATE with a proposed A44.5 row in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` + a `SendMessage` to `main`. MUST NOT silently drop.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§6.5 record 2026-08-25 (APPROVED owner) — prong 2 + Q3 sunset">MUST NOT alter `Dataverse-ClientSecret` manifest entry. It STAYS unconditionally as Q3 Path A time-boxed rollback copy until 2026-11-23 sunset. Similarly, MUST NOT reclassify `FromBicepOutput` / `FromExistingKvSecret` / `FromRunParameter` / `Generated` value-source classification for entries that STAY (Cosmos, `Dataverse-ClientSecret`, `Dataverse-ServiceUrl`, `SPE-ContainerTypeId`, `AzureOpenAI-ApiKey`, `Communication-Webhook-SigningKey`) — only the three omit-target entries change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §3 Sub-Agent Write Boundary">Edits to `.claude/**` (e.g. `.claude/constraints/provisioning.md` §6.5 EDIT package prong 1 rewrite, if not yet landed) MUST occur in the MAIN SESSION. A38 code edits are safe for sub-agent execution; document any `.claude/**` follow-up as a coord item — do NOT attempt from a sub-agent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11 component justification">Any NEW file created (e.g. a `ManifestLinter.cs` or `SecretFreeEnvMarker.cs` if separated for testability, OR a new test file) MUST cite punch row A38 in the file header + answer Existing/Extension/Cost-of-doing-nothing. Prefer EXTENDING `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs` + `FileKvSecretManifest.cs` over new sibling files.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §Human Escalation Triggers + row A38 partial-omit trap">If ANY of the three secret entries is discovered to have MULTIPLE upsert sites beyond `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs:74` (e.g. also in `FileKvSecretManifest`, `Rotate-Secrets.ps1`, `Configure-ProductionAppSettings.ps1`, `Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1`, or a Bicep `listKeys()` deployment output), STOP + re-scope. An incomplete omit-set is worse than no change — a residual site keeps the sentinel-vs-omit fight going + falsely reports "migrated" in the run record.</constraint>
    <constraint source="remediation plan §5 item 3 + auth-v4 §10.5 trap 2">If executor discovers `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1`'s silent admin-key fallback ("KV secret AiSearch--AdminKey not found — falling back to live admin key") is triggered as a side effect of omitting `AiSearch--AdminKey`, DO NOT fix that path here — it is punch row A43's scope (Phase-F, not 186-blocking). Note in run report + amend punch list annotation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="verification obligation (post-A35 re-verify)">If the manifest generator has been refactored since 2026-08-25 (last grep-verify), re-verify `FromBicepOutput` classification for all three entries BEFORE editing. Grep for `AiSearch--AdminKey` + `BFF-API-ClientSecret` + `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` across `src/server/services/**` + `infrastructure/bicep/**` + `scripts/**` and record all hits in scratchpad before any edit.</constraint>
  </constraints>

