  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL block (FULL, xhigh effort, Fable/Opus). Read `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` row A38 verbatim. Read `notes/auth-v4-integration-remediation-plan.md` §5 (silent-failure catalog — item 3 migration-undo vectors + SF-16 sentinel), §7 (sequencing — A38 ∥ A42 → A39), §8 (effort). Read `notes/decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md` §Owner refinements + §Path C rationale. Read `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs`, `FileKvSecretManifest.cs`, `IKvSecretManifest.cs` in full. Read H4 handler bodies (`H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs`, `H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs`) to understand Model 1 (shared) vs Model 2 (per-customer) dispatch.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Grep-verify current state BEFORE applying">Run grep across `src/server/services/**` + `infrastructure/bicep/**` + `scripts/**` for each of the three secret names: `AiSearch--AdminKey` (verified present at `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs:74`), `BFF-API-ClientSecret` (source site TBD), `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` (source site TBD). Record every hit in scratchpad table (file:line + operation context: upsert/read/rotate/seed). Grep for `skip-if-absent` + `never-declared` + `never_declared` to confirm A23 clobber guard is present + record its test coverage. Grep for `Dataverse-ClientSecret` to confirm the Path A entry is still present (MUST NOT be affected by A38). Also grep for existing test files covering `StaticKvSecretManifest` / `FileKvSecretManifest` / `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler` / `H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler` to identify test-modify targets.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Escalation trigger check — partial-omit trap">If Step 1 found MULTIPLE upsert sites for any of the three secrets beyond the manifest generator (e.g. also in `Rotate-Secrets.ps1`, `Configure-ProductionAppSettings.ps1`, `Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1`, `customer.bicep:~667/:675`, or Bicep `listKeys()` deployment outputs), STOP. Escalate with the exact site inventory + a re-scoped omit set. An incomplete omit-set is worse than no change. If only the manifest generator is a live upsert path (other hits are read-only or `SkipIfAbsent`-guarded), proceed.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Design the secret-free-env branch + marker mechanism">Author (in scratchpad first, then code) the design: (a) how the manifest generator DETECTS "secret-free env" — options: (i) `KvSecretsPopulationOptions.RequireSecretFreeIdentity` flag, (ii) KV resource tag probe, (iii) run-parameter from operator intake. Recommendation: mirror `Graph__Credentials__RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` App Service setting via a new `KvSecretsPopulationOptions.RequireSecretFreeIdentity` bool + a run-parameter override (`explicitRollback: true` re-includes the three entries under Q3 Path A). (b) WHERE the migration marker is applied — KV resource tag `spaarke-secret-free-identity=true` OR `sprk_dataverseenvironment` state field `sprk_credentialmode=secret-free`. Recommendation: BOTH (tag on KV for infra-scan detectability; state field for provisioning-run auditability). Document the choice in code comments referencing §9.1.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Checkpoint (after 4 steps)">Run `context-handoff` (silent: "Checkpoint.").</step>
    <step order="5" name="Apply omit edits — manifest source(s)">Edit `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs` (line 74 area — the `AiSearch--AdminKey` entry, and the `BFF-API-ClientSecret` entry at line 69 IF the row is the live upsert path per Step 1 verification). Also edit any additional manifest source discovered in Step 1 (`FileKvSecretManifest.cs` if it lists these entries in its default YAML/JSON, or wherever else). Wrap the three entries in a `if (!options.RequireSecretFreeIdentity)` conditional. Update the file header comment block explaining §9.1 OMIT-is-the-signal contract, cite row A38 + remediation plan §5 item 3, cite §6.5 record's per-secret disposition. PRESERVE `Dataverse-ClientSecret` unconditionally (Q3 Path A). PRESERVE `Cosmos*` / `SPE-ContainerTypeId` / `AzureOpenAI-ApiKey` / `Communication-Webhook-SigningKey` / `Dataverse-ServiceUrl` unchanged (their value-source classification is out of scope).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Apply marker mechanism">Extend `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler` + `H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler` to apply the positive migration marker per Step 3 design (KV resource tag + `sprk_dataverseenvironment` state field). Marker application is idempotent (re-run yields same state). For Model 2, marker application is invoked ONCE PER VAULT in the fan-out loop (the handlers already iterate per-customer for Model 2; hook the marker into that iteration). Log marker application at Information level with vault ID for fleet-consistency auditing.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Add H7/task-142 half — A30 sentinel contract closure OR escalation">Grep-locate the H7/task-142 sentinel surface. If it lives in the same handler family (`H7*` under `Handlers/**`), apply the equivalent OMIT contract + marker per the same design. If it is a substantially different surface (e.g. env-var manifest, not KV manifest) requiring its own POML + reviewer attention, ESCALATE with a proposed A44.5 row in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` + `SendMessage` to `main` — do NOT silently drop. Record disposition in scratchpad.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Checkpoint (after 3 steps of edits)">Run `context-handoff` (silent: "Checkpoint.").</step>
