  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11 three-question template). **Existing**: `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs` (interim per Phase-H task 084) is the current authoritative manifest source; `FileKvSecretManifest.cs` is the Phase-H replacement seam; `H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler` + `H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler` are the Model 1 vs Model 2 dispatch points; `KvSecretsPopulationOptions` is the existing options envelope; A23's clobber-guard mechanism (skip-if-absent + never-declared) is already in this manifest area. A38 EXTENDS these — no new sibling components. **Extension**: Adding a `RequireSecretFreeIdentity` bool to `KvSecretsPopulationOptions` + wrapping three `KvSecretEntry(...)` items in a conditional + adding a marker-application code path to H4/H4-shared handlers. If a `ManifestLinter.cs` is separated for testability of the Model 2 fleet-consistency detector, its file header cites A38 + §5.3 fleet-consistency gap + answers Existing/Extension/Cost. **Cost-of-doing-nothing**: A38 is BLOCKS-186 per remediation plan §7 (auth-v4 §10.1 Δ1+Δ2 + §9.1 sentinel ruling). Concrete failure modes without A38: (1) fresh Model 2 customer boots on FIC (per Δ3 A39 settings) but H4 STILL upserts admin-key + client-secret + SB conn-string → the "secret beneath MI-FIC absorbing a broken FIC with green health" failure mode (remediation plan §8) — the single failure mode auth-v4 identified as "strictly worse than no migration"; (2) A38 also blocks A39 (§10.2 ordering guard — cannot set `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` at App Service if manifest still surfaces the secret slot in KV, boot-loops the stamp); (3) migration-undo vector remediation plan §5 item 3 stays live — every H4 run silently reverses the auth-v4 migration while reporting green. Rule: prong 3 of §6.5 record narrows to `spaarkedev1` + any as-yet-unprovisioned Model 2 stamp; per Q6, no Model 2 stamp will be provisioned before A36-A42 land — so A38's omit contract holds for 100% of new provisioning traffic.</notes>

